(/***********************************************************************) 81 642 T
( *) 81 631 T
(Class & Method Definitions) 212.5 631 T
( * This section contains the definition of the application\325s Process) 81 620 T
( * class and its methods. Other classes can also be defined here,) 81 609 T
( * along with the message each handles.) 81 598 T
( ***********************************************************************/) 81 587 T
(/*) 81 569 T
( * Here we define \322HelloProcessClass\323 as a subclass of the system-provided) 81 558 T
( * \322GenProcessClass\323. As this application is launched, an instance of this class) 81 547 T
( * will be created automatically to handle application-related events \050messages\051.) 81 536 T
( * The application thread will be responsible for running this object,) 81 525 T
( * meaning that whenever this object handles a message, it will be executing) 81 514 T
( * in the application\325s thread.) 81 503 T
( */) 81 492 T
(/* You will find no object in this file declared to be of this class. Instead,) 81 474 T
( * this class is bound to the application thread in hello3.gp.) 81 463 T
(@class HelloProcessClass, GenProcessClass;) 81 445 T
(/* The messages HelloProcessClass objects can handle that are not) 81 427 T
( * system-defined are enumerated here. Each of these messages is sent) 81 416 T
( * by one of the triggers in the dialog box. This is where class-) 81 405 T
( * specific messages for this application \050not system-defined messages\051) 81 394 T
( * are defined. */) 81 383 T
(@message void MSG_HELLO_CHANGE_TO_BLUE\050\051; /* sent by Blue trigger */) 81 365 T
(@message void MSG_HELLO_CHANGE_TO_GOLD\050\051; /* sent by Gold trigger */) 81 354 T
(@message void MSG_HELLO_REDRAW_DOCUMENT\050\051; /* sent by Process to itself */) 81 343 T
(@endc /* signifies end of class definition */) 81 325 T
(/* Because this class definition must be stored in memory at runtime,) 81 307 T
( * we must declare it here along with a flag indicating how it should) 81 296 T
( * be loaded. The \322neverSaved\323 flag is used because Process classes) 81 285 T
( * are never saved to state files and therefore no relocation tables) 81 274 T
( * need be built. */) 81 263 T
(@classdecl HelloProcessClass, neverSaved;) 81 252 T
