2 18 Q
(Cooperative Multitasking) 189 320 T
3 10 Q
-0.01 (A cooperative multitasking system, as the name suggests, is one in which) 189 296.33 P
(the various programs cooperate. They agree to share the system and its) 189 283.33 T
(resources. Each program running under a system has complete control) 189 270.33 T
(while it is actually running. Every so often, when it reaches a convenient) 189 257.33 T
(place, it calls a special system routine \050called a context-switch routine\051 to) 189 244.33 T
(see if any other program has work do to. If so, that program takes control) 189 231.33 T
(of the system until it in turn reaches a convenient stopping point and) 189 218.33 T
(passes control on to the next waiting program. If several programs are) 189 205.33 T
(ready to run, they wait in a queue so that each one gets a chance to run) 189 192.33 T
(before the \336rst program runs again. \050It is also possible to implement a) 189 179.33 T
(cooperative multitasking system where some programs have a higher) 189 166.33 T
(priority than others. In this case, a more complicated algorithm might be) 189 153.33 T
